{title: Praise to the Lord, the Almighty}
{artist: Joachim Neander (1680); tr. Catherine Winkworth (1863)}
{key: G}
{tempo: 96}
{time: 3/4}
{meta: tune LOBE DEN HERREN - Stralsund Gesangbuch (1665)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1863, tune 1665: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Praise to the [Em]Lord, the Al[D]mighty, the [G]King of cre[D]ation!
[G]O my soul, [Em]praise Him, for [D]He is thy [G]health and sal[D]vation!
[G]All ye who [D]hear, [Em]now to His [C]temple draw [D]near;
[G]Praise Him in [C]glad ado[D]ra[G]tion.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Praise to the [Em]Lord, who o'er [D]all things so [G]wondrously [D]reigneth,
[G]Shelters thee [Em]under His [D]wings, yea, so [G]gently sus[D]taineth!
[G]Hast thou not [D]seen [Em]how thy de[C]sires e'er have [D]been
[G]Granted in [C]what He or[D]dain[G]eth?
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Praise to the [Em]Lord! O let [D]all that is [G]in me a[D]dore Him!
[G]All that hath [Em]life and breath, [D]come now with [G]praises be[D]fore Him.
[G]Let the A[D]men [Em]sound from His [C]people a[D]gain:
[G]Gladly for[C]aye we a[D]dore [G]Him.
{end_of_verse}
